IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rtw-dates`
IMPORT `rtw-core`

-- Return to Work Act 1986 (NT) -- the employer's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the employer of an injured worker, read with its insurer; where the employer is uninsured, the Nominal Insurer
-- stands in its place for the claim decisions (s 85(10)). The text puts hard working-day deadlines on this party (ss 84,
-- 85, 87, 88), so it has a seat of its own, beside the worker's in rtw-seat.l4. "Must I compensate this worker? How much,
-- and until when? By when must I forward, decide and pay? Am I taken to have accepted? May I dismiss, or recover an
-- overpayment? What is the most I can be fined?" The rules are in rtw-core.l4; this module builds the core's records from
-- plain answers and restates no rule. Its names differ from the worker seat's, so a case file can import both.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Return to Work Act -- the employer's questions`

GIVEN a1 IS A BOOLEAN, a2 IS A BOOLEAN, a3 IS A BOOLEAN, a4 IS A BOOLEAN, a5 IS A BOOLEAN, a6 IS A BOOLEAN, a7 IS A BOOLEAN
      a8 IS A BOOLEAN, a9 IS A BOOLEAN, a10 IS A BOOLEAN, a11 IS A BOOLEAN, a12 IS A BOOLEAN, a13 IS A NUMBER
      a14 IS A `Prescribed class`
GIVETH A `Worker facts`
`the facts about this person` a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 a7 a8 a9 a10 a11 a12 a13 a14 MEANS
    `Worker facts` WITH
        `works for another person under a contract`                                              IS a1
        `is an employee under the PAYG provisions, or should be`                                  IS a2
        `is employed by the Commonwealth`                                                         IS a3
        `employs another person in the work`                                                      IS a4
        `is engaged other than for the purposes of the employer's trade, business or enterprise`  IS a5
        `the employer makes PAYG withholding payments for the person`                             IS a6
        `is a prescribed family member of the employer and lives with the employer`               IS a7
        `is a director of the body corporate that employs the person`                              IS a8
        `PAYG is withheld from the director's remuneration`                                       IS a9
        `the person's details were disclosed to the employer's insurer as s 3B(4) or (6)(b) requires` IS a10
        `is employed or engaged by a householder`                                                 IS a11
        `is under the contract a contestant in a sporting or athletic activity, or training or travelling for one` IS a12
        `yearly remuneration`                                                                     IS a13
        `prescribed class`                                                                        IS a14

§§ `Must I compensate this worker?`

@export Is this person my worker under the Return to Work Act 1986 (NT) (s 3B, regs 3A, 4, 4A, 5)?
GIVEN `the person works for me under a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person does work or a service of any kind for you under a contract, written or not
      `the person is my employee for PAYG withholding, or should be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, for this work, the person is your employee for PAYG withholding, or should be treated as one even if you do not (an ABN does not decide it)
      `the person is employed by the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is employed by the Commonwealth
      `the person employs someone else in the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person employs another person to do the work in question
      `I engage the person other than for my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you engage the person other than for the purposes of your trade, business or enterprise
      `I withhold PAYG tax for the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you make PAYG withholding payments for the person
      `the person is a close family member who lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is your spouse, parent, grandparent, child, grandchild, brother or sister (including step and half relations) and lives with you
      `the person is a director of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is a director of the body corporate that employs them
      `I withhold PAYG from the director's pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is a director, whether PAYG tax is withheld from what the company pays them
      `I disclosed the person to my insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is a family member living with you, or a director, whether you disclosed their name, the nature of the work and estimated pay to your insurer at the start (or when the insurance began) and at each renewal
      `I am a householder employing the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you employ or engage the person as a householder (privately, in your home)
      `I pay the person as a sports contestant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is for the person to take part as a contestant in a sporting or athletic activity, or to train or travel for one
      `the person's yearly pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay the person in a year, or the yearly equivalent of the rate, in Australian dollars
      `the person's prescribed class` IS A `Prescribed class` @desc Whether reg 3A names the person's kind of work as a worker, as not a worker, or neither
      `average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The NT average weekly earnings figure in force, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person my worker under the Return to Work Act` IF
    `the person is a worker under s 3B` (`the facts about this person` `the person works for me under a contract` `the person is my employee for PAYG withholding, or should be` `the person is employed by the Commonwealth` `the person employs someone else in the work` `I engage the person other than for my business` `I withhold PAYG tax for the person` `the person is a close family member who lives with me` `the person is a director of my company` `I withhold PAYG from the director's pay` `I disclosed the person to my insurer` `I am a householder employing the person` `I pay the person as a sports contestant` `the person's yearly pay` `the person's prescribed class`) `average weekly earnings`

@export Must I compensate this worker for this injury, and if not, why not (ss 3A, 3B, 4, 53, 53AA, 57, 58, 60)?
GIVEN `the person works for me under a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person does work or a service of any kind for you under a contract
      `the person is my employee for PAYG withholding, or should be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is your employee for PAYG withholding, or should be
      `the person is employed by the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is employed by the Commonwealth
      `the person employs someone else in the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person employs another person to do the work in question
      `I engage the person other than for my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you engage the person other than for the purposes of your trade, business or enterprise
      `I withhold PAYG tax for the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you make PAYG withholding payments for the person
      `the person is a close family member who lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is a close family member who lives with you
      `the person is a director of my company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is a director of the body corporate that employs them
      `I withhold PAYG from the director's pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a director, whether PAYG tax is withheld from their pay
      `I disclosed the person to my insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a family member living with you or a director, whether you disclosed them to your insurer as s 3B requires
      `I am a householder employing the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you employ the person as a householder
      `I pay the person as a sports contestant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is for the person to take part as a sports contestant, or to train or travel for it
      `the person's yearly pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay the person in a year, or its yearly equivalent, in dollars
      `the person's prescribed class` IS A `Prescribed class` @desc Whether reg 3A names the person's kind of work as a worker, as not a worker, or neither
      `where the worker usually works for me` IS A `Jurisdiction` @desc Where the worker usually works in this employment (last 12 months and intentions; ignore a temporary stint elsewhere of 6 months or less)
      `where the worker is usually based` IS A `Jurisdiction` @desc Where the worker is usually based for this employment
      `where my main place of business in Australia is` IS A `Jurisdiction` @desc Where your principal place of business in Australia is (your ABN address; "no one jurisdiction" if none in Australia)
      `the worker was in the Territory when injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was in the Northern Territory when injured
      `a country outside Australia may compensate the worker for this` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law of a place outside Australia may entitle the worker to compensation for the same injury
      `the injury arose out of or in the course of the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the physical or mental injury (including a disease, or making an earlier one worse) arose out of or in the course of the employment (s 4)
      `it is a mental injury caused mainly by my reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a mental injury caused wholly or mainly by management action you took on reasonable grounds and in a reasonable way, a reasonable decision about such action, or the worker's expectation of it
      `it happened in a motor accident on a journey or a break` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it happened in a motor accident on a break, or on a journey s 4(2A) leaves to the motor accidents scheme
      `it caused death, impairment or incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury resulted in, or materially contributed to, death, an impairment or an inability to work
      `it is a heart attack or stroke` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a heart attack or stroke injury
      `the work materially contributed to the heart attack or stroke` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a heart attack or stroke, whether the employment was its real, proximate or effective cause
      `the worker deliberately self-inflicted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was deliberately self-inflicted
      `it was caused by the worker's serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is attributable to the worker's serious and wilful misconduct
      `it caused death or permanent or long-term incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury resulted in death or a permanent or long-term inability to work
      `the worker was driving a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was driving a motor vehicle when injured
      `the worker had been drinking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker had consumed alcohol before driving
      `the worker's blood alcohol reading` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's blood alcohol concentration in grams per 100 millilitres (or breath alcohol per 210 litres); 0 if none was measured
      `the drinking is found to have materially contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has been found that the drinking materially contributed to the accident
      `the worker proved the alcohol did not contribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the reading was 0.08 or more, whether the worker has proved the alcohol did not materially contribute
      `the worker was under the influence of a drug` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was driving under the influence of a drug
      `average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The NT average weekly earnings figure in force, in dollars
GIVETH A `Coverage answer`
`Must I compensate this worker for this injury` MEANS
    `whether the injury is compensable`
        (`the facts about this person` `the person works for me under a contract` `the person is my employee for PAYG withholding, or should be` `the person is employed by the Commonwealth` `the person employs someone else in the work` `I engage the person other than for my business` `I withhold PAYG tax for the person` `the person is a close family member who lives with me` `the person is a director of my company` `I withhold PAYG from the director's pay` `I disclosed the person to my insurer` `I am a householder employing the person` `I pay the person as a sports contestant` `the person's yearly pay` `the person's prescribed class`)
        (`Connection facts` WITH
            `where the worker usually works in the employment`                      IS `where the worker usually works for me`
            `where the worker is usually based for the employment`                  IS `where the worker is usually based`
            `where the employer's principal place of business in Australia is`      IS `where my main place of business in Australia is`
            `the worker was in the Territory when injured`                          IS `the worker was in the Territory when injured`
            `a place outside Australia may compensate the worker for the same matter` IS `a country outside Australia may compensate the worker for this`)
        (`Injury facts` WITH
            `arose out of or in the course of the employment`                                         IS `the injury arose out of or in the course of the work`
            `is a mental injury caused wholly or primarily by reasonable management action`           IS `it is a mental injury caused mainly by my reasonable management action`
            `was sustained in a motor accident that s 4(2A) takes out of the employment`               IS `it happened in a motor accident on a journey or a break`
            `resulted in or materially contributed to death, impairment or incapacity`                IS `it caused death, impairment or incapacity`
            `is a heart attack or stroke injury`                                                      IS `it is a heart attack or stroke`
            `the employment materially contributed to the heart attack or stroke`                     IS `the work materially contributed to the heart attack or stroke`
            `was deliberately self-inflicted`                                                         IS `the worker deliberately self-inflicted it`
            `is attributable to the worker's serious and wilful misconduct`                           IS `it was caused by the worker's serious and wilful misconduct`
            `resulted in death or permanent or long-term incapacity`                                  IS `it caused death or permanent or long-term incapacity`
            `was sustained while the worker was driving a motor vehicle`                              IS `the worker was driving a motor vehicle`
            `the worker had consumed alcoholic liquor`                                                IS `the worker had been drinking`
            `the worker's alcohol concentration, in grams per 100 millilitres of blood or per 210 litres of breath` IS `the worker's blood alcohol reading`
            `the consumption is found to have materially contributed to the accident`                 IS `the drinking is found to have materially contributed`
            `the contrary of the s 60(2) presumption is proved`                                       IS `the worker proved the alcohol did not contribute`
            `the worker was under the influence of a drug`                                            IS `the worker was under the influence of a drug`)
        `average weekly earnings`

§§ `How much must I pay, and until when?`

@export How much weekly compensation must I pay this worker for this week (ss 64, 65, 65A, 65B, 61A)?
GIVEN `the weeks of weekly compensation already paid for this injury` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of weekly compensation have already been paid for this injury, in total (a part week counts as a week); 0 for the first week
      `a doctor certifies the worker unfit this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a medical practitioner certifies the worker totally or partly incapacitated for work this week because of the injury (needed in the first 26 weeks)
      `the worker's whole person impairment is 15% or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker's permanent impairment, assessed as for s 72 and leaving out a psychological impairment that follows a physical injury, is 15% or more of the whole person
      `the worker's normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's normal weekly earnings immediately before compensation began (s 49A), in dollars
      `what the worker actually earned from work this week` IS A NUMBER @desc What the worker actually earned in employment this week, in dollars
      `the worker's indexed normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc After 26 weeks: the worker's normal weekly earnings indexed under s 65(3), in dollars (the s 65(3A) formula is missing from the deposited text)
      `what the worker could reasonably earn in a week` IS A NUMBER @desc After 26 weeks: what the worker is reasonably capable of earning in a week in the most profitable work reasonably available (first 104 weeks) or that the worker could do (after 104 weeks), in dollars; 0 if nothing
      `the worker's spouse is wholly or mainly dependent on the worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker's spouse or de facto partner was, at the injury and now, wholly or mainly dependent on the worker
      `the worker's number of prescribed children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the worker's children are under 16, or 16 to 20 and studying full time or handicapped, and not married
      `the worker's spouse's normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's spouse's normal weekly earnings, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the worker is in prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker is a prisoner (or detained, or in like circumstances, outside the Territory) and someone is liable to maintain them
      `the worker lives outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker now lives outside Australia
      `the worker gives me the reg 6A declarations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the worker lives abroad, whether the worker gives you the reg 6A declarations by the worker and a doctor
      `I am satisfied the worker is still incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the worker lives abroad, whether you are satisfied the worker remains incapacitated
      `the Court has extended the worker's payments abroad` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the worker lives abroad and 104 weeks have been paid, whether a Court extension covers this week
      `average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The NT average weekly earnings figure in force, in dollars
GIVETH A `Weekly compensation answer`
`How much weekly compensation must I pay this worker this week` MEANS
    `the weekly compensation for the week`
        (`Week facts` WITH
            `the weeks of weekly payments already paid for the injury`                         IS `the weeks of weekly compensation already paid for this injury`
            `a medical practitioner certifies the worker incapacitated for the week`           IS `a doctor certifies the worker unfit this week`
            `the worker's relevant permanent impairment is 15% or more`                        IS `the worker's whole person impairment is 15% or more`
            `normal weekly earnings`                                                           IS `the worker's normal weekly earnings`
            `the amount the worker actually earned in employment during the week`              IS `what the worker actually earned from work this week`
            `the worker is a prisoner, or detained outside the Territory, and someone is liable to maintain the worker` IS `the worker is in prison`
            `the worker lives outside Australia`                                               IS `the worker lives outside Australia`
            `the worker gives the reg 6A declarations`                                         IS `the worker gives me the reg 6A declarations`
            `the employer is satisfied about the worker's continued incapacity`                IS `I am satisfied the worker is still incapacitated`
            `a Court order under s 65B(4) extends the entitlement for the week`                IS `the Court has extended the worker's payments abroad`
            `long-term facts`                                                                  IS
                `Long-term incapacity facts` WITH
                    `indexed normal weekly earnings`                                   IS `the worker's indexed normal weekly earnings`
                    `the amount the worker is reasonably capable of earning in a week`  IS `what the worker could reasonably earn in a week`
                    `the worker's spouse is wholly or mainly dependent on the worker`   IS `the worker's spouse is wholly or mainly dependent on the worker`
                    `the number of the worker's prescribed children`                    IS `the worker's number of prescribed children`
                    `the worker's spouse's normal weekly earnings`                      IS `the worker's spouse's normal weekly earnings`)
        `average weekly earnings`

@export Until when must I pay this worker's weekly compensation (s 65(1BA), (1D))?
GIVEN `the worker's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The worker's date of birth
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The date of the injury that caused (or contributed to) the incapacity
      `the worker's pension age in months` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's age pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) s 23, in months (804 for 67 years)
      `the usual retiring age in the worker's industry, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc The age at which workers in the worker's industry or occupation usually retire, in months
      `the worker's whole person impairment is 15% or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker's relevant permanent impairment is 15% or more of the whole person
GIVETH A `Payment period answer`
`Until when must I pay this worker's weekly compensation` MEANS
    `the period of s 65 compensation under s 65(1D)`
        (`Period facts` WITH
            `the worker's date of birth`                                          IS `the worker's date of birth`
            `the injury date`                                                     IS `the day of the injury`
            `the worker's future pension age, in months`                          IS `the worker's pension age in months`
            `the normal retiring age in the worker's industry or occupation, in months` IS `the usual retiring age in the worker's industry, in months`
            `the worker's relevant permanent impairment is 15% or more`           IS `the worker's whole person impairment is 15% or more`)

@export What permanent impairment compensation must I pay this worker (ss 70, 71)?
GIVEN `the worker's assessed whole person impairment, in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's permanent impairment as assessed under the approved guides, as a percentage of the whole person (14 for 14%)
      `average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The NT average weekly earnings figure at the time of payment, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Impairment lump sum answer`
`What permanent impairment compensation must I pay this worker` MEANS
    `the permanent impairment compensation under s 71` `the worker's assessed whole person impairment, in per cent` `average weekly earnings`

@export By when must I pay this worker's permanent impairment compensation (s 71(4))?
GIVEN `the day the worker was notified of the assessment` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker was told of the medical practitioner's assessment
      `a reassessment was applied for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reassessment was applied for within the 28 days
      `the day the applicant was notified of the reassessment` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the applicant was notified of the panel's reassessment (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I pay this worker's permanent impairment compensation` MEANS
    IF `a reassessment was applied for`
    THEN `the last day to pay under s 71(4)(b)` `the day the applicant was notified of the reassessment`
    ELSE `the last day to pay under s 71(4)(a)` `the day the worker was notified of the assessment`

§§ `What must I do on a claim, and by when?`
-- Situation: you have received a claim for compensation.

@export Where must I forward this claim (s 84(1))?
GIVEN `my insurance position` IS AN `Insurance position` @desc Whether you are "insured with an approved insurer", "a self-insurer", or "uninsured"
GIVETH A `Forwarding answer`
`Where must I forward this claim` MEANS `where the claim must be forwarded under s 84(1)` `my insurance position`

@export By when must I forward this claim (s 84(1))?
GIVEN `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the claim
      `weekday public holidays in the next 3 working days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Territory public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the days after that, before the deadline (usually 0)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I forward this claim` MEANS
    `the last day to forward the claim under s 84(1)` `the day I received the claim` `weekday public holidays in the next 3 working days`

@export By when must I notify the claimant that I accept, defer or dispute liability (s 85(1))? If I do not, I am taken to have accepted (s 87)
GIVEN `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the claim
      `weekday public holidays in the next 10 working days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Territory public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the two weeks or so after that (usually 0)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I decide this claim` MEANS
    `the last day to notify a decision under s 85(1)` `the day I received the claim` `weekday public holidays in the next 10 working days`

@export By when must I start weekly payments after accepting or deferring this claim (s 85(2), (4)(b))?
GIVEN `the day I accepted or deferred` IS A DATE @desc The day you decided to accept, or to defer accepting, liability for a claim for weekly payments
      `weekday public holidays in the next 3 working days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Territory public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the days after that (usually 0)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I start this worker's weekly payments` MEANS
    `the last day to commence weekly payments under s 85(2) or (4)(b)` `the day I accepted or deferred` `weekday public holidays in the next 3 working days`

@export Until when does my deferral of this claim last (s 85(4)(a))?
GIVEN `the day my deferral notice was given or posted` IS A DATE @desc The day your written notice of deferral was given to the claimant or posted
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when does my deferral last` MEANS
    `the last day of a deferral under s 85(4)(a)` `the day my deferral notice was given or posted`

@export Am I taken to have accepted liability for this claim (s 87)?
GIVEN `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the claim
      `weekday public holidays in the next 10 working days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Territory public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the two weeks or so after that (usually 0)
      `I have notified a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have notified the claimant in writing that you accept, defer or dispute liability
      `the day I notified it` IS A DATE @desc The day that notice was given or posted (any date if none)
      `my decision` IS A `Liability decision` @desc What you decided: accept, defer, dispute with the s 85(8) statement, or dispute without it
      `after deferring, I have accepted or properly disputed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you deferred, whether you have since notified acceptance, or a dispute with the s 85(8) statement
      `the day I notified that` IS A DATE @desc The day that later notice was given or posted (any date if none)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Deemed acceptance answer`
`Am I taken to have accepted this claim` MEANS
    `whether liability is deemed accepted under s 87`
        (`Decision facts` WITH
            `the day the employer received the claim`                         IS `the day I received the claim`
            `weekday public holidays in the 10 working days`                  IS `weekday public holidays in the next 10 working days`
            `the employer has notified a decision`                            IS `I have notified a decision`
            `the day the decision was notified or posted`                     IS `the day I notified it`
            `the decision`                                                    IS `my decision`
            `after deferring, the employer has notified acceptance or a dispute with the s 85(8) statement` IS `after deferring, I have accepted or properly disputed`
            `the day that later decision was notified or posted`              IS `the day I notified that`
            `today`                                                           IS `today`)

@export Does my notice disputing this claim meet s 85(8) and (9), so that it counts as a decision (s 87(3)), and reg 13?
GIVEN `my statement is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your statement is in the approved form
      `my statement gives reasons the claimant can fully understand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it gives the reasons in enough detail for the claimant to understand fully why you dispute liability
      `my statement gives the 90 days for mediation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it says the claimant may apply to the Authority for mediation within 90 days
      `my statement says the claimant may then go to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it says the claimant may start Court proceedings if mediation fails
      `my statement gives the 28 days after the mediator's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it says a Court application must be lodged within 28 days after the mediator's certificate
      `my statement says mediation must come first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it says proceedings may be started only after an unsuccessful mediation
      `my statement mentions an interim determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it says the claimant may seek an interim determination once mediation is applied for
      `I gave it with my notice of dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the statement at the same time as notifying the dispute
      `I gave a copy and the mediation information bulletin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you also gave the worker a copy of the statement and the approved information bulletin on mediation (reg 13)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my dispute notice meet s 85(8) and reg 13` IF
        `the statement meets s 85(8) and (9)` `my statement facts`
    AND `the employer also met reg 13` `my statement facts`
    WHERE
        `my statement facts` MEANS
            `Dispute statement facts` WITH
                `is in the approved form`                                                             IS `my statement is in the approved form`
                `sets out the reasons in enough detail for the claimant to understand fully why`      IS `my statement gives reasons the claimant can fully understand`
                `says the claimant may apply to the Authority for mediation within 90 days`           IS `my statement gives the 90 days for mediation`
                `says the claimant may go to the Court if mediation does not resolve the dispute`     IS `my statement says the claimant may then go to the Court`
                `says a Court application must be lodged within 28 days after the mediator's certificate` IS `my statement gives the 28 days after the mediator's certificate`
                `says proceedings may be started only after an unsuccessful mediation`                IS `my statement says mediation must come first`
                `says an interim determination may be sought once mediation is applied for`           IS `my statement mentions an interim determination`
                `was given at the same time as the notice of the dispute`                             IS `I gave it with my notice of dispute`
                `came with a copy of the statement and the approved information bulletin on mediation` IS `I gave a copy and the mediation information bulletin`

§§ `What must I do while paying, and by when?`
-- Situation: you are paying weekly compensation.

@export By when must I make this weekly payment (s 88(1))? Late payment carries s 89 interest and is an offence
GIVEN `the last day of the week the payment is for` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the week (or of the worker's normal longer pay period) the payment is for
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I make this weekly payment` MEANS
    `the last day to make the weekly payment under s 88(1)` `the last day of the week the payment is for`

@export How many weeks late was this weekly payment, for the s 89 interest I must add?
GIVEN `the day the payment was due` IS A DATE @desc The last day on which the weekly payment should have been made
      `the day I paid it` IS A DATE @desc The day you actually paid it
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many weeks late was this weekly payment` MEANS
    `B, the weeks late under s 89(1)` `the day the payment was due` `the day I paid it`

@export By when must I give this worker the earnings information they asked for (s 85A)?
GIVEN `the day I received the request` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's request for information about their weekly earnings
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I give this worker earnings information` MEANS
    `the last day to give earnings information under s 85A(2)` `the day I received the request`

@export By when must I decide this worker's application to change their weekly payments (s 86)?
GIVEN `the day I received the application` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's application to increase or decrease weekly payments
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I decide this worker's application` MEANS
    `the last day to decide an application to alter weekly payments under s 86(2)` `the day I received the application`

@export When does the change take effect, after my notice of a statutory event (s 61B(4))?
GIVEN `the day I gave or posted the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day your written notice of the statutory event was given to the worker or posted
      `the day of the statutory event` IS A DATE @desc The day of the event (the end of the first 26 weeks, of the 260 weeks or of the 104 weeks, or the worker reaching retiring age or pension age)
GIVETH A DATE
`When does my notice of a statutory event take effect` MEANS
    `the day the change takes effect under s 61B(4)` `the day I gave or posted the notice` `the day of the statutory event`

@export Would dismissing this worker be an offence under s 65C?
GIVEN `the worker is unable to work, fully or partly, because of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker is totally or partially incapacitated for work as a result of the injury
      `the reason would be the worker's serious misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the reason for the dismissal is the worker's serious misconduct, as s 65C(4) defines it
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker was injured
      `the day of the dismissal` IS A DATE @desc The day of the dismissal (including the worker leaving because of an unreasonable condition designed to make them leave)
GIVETH A `Dismissal answer`
`Would dismissing this worker be an offence` MEANS
    `whether a dismissal is an offence under s 65C` `the worker is unable to work, fully or partly, because of the injury` `the reason would be the worker's serious misconduct` `the day of the injury` `the day of the dismissal`

@export Can I recover this overpayment from the worker (s 74)?
GIVEN `I calculated the benefit incorrectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your insurer calculated the benefit incorrectly
      `the last day of the period the payment was for` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period the overpaid amount was paid for
      `the day I sought to recover it` IS A DATE @desc The day you first sought to recover the overpaid amount
GIVETH AN `Overpayment answer`
`Can I recover this overpayment` MEANS
    `whether the overpayment can be recovered under s 74` `I calculated the benefit incorrectly` `the last day of the period the payment was for` `the day I sought to recover it`

@export What is the most I can be fined for an offence about a claim or weekly payments (ss 65C, 84(5), 85A, 86, 88), in penalty units?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Employer offence` @desc Which offence
      `I am a company or other body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body corporate rather than an individual
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined` MEANS
    `the maximum penalty in penalty units for` `the offence` `I am a company or other body corporate`

@export May I now reduce or cancel this worker's weekly compensation for not undertaking treatment, rehabilitation or an assessment (ss 75B, 69)?
GIVEN `the worker's failure or refusal was unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is found that the worker unreasonably failed to undertake reasonable treatment, training or a return to work program, or unreasonably refused an assessment you required
      `days since I gave notice of the cut` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days ago you gave the worker written notice of the intended reduction or cancellation (0 if none)
      `I gave the s 69 statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you also gave the statement in the approved form with reasons and the worker's mediation rights
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I cut this worker's weekly compensation for not undertaking treatment` IF
    `weekly compensation may now be reduced or cancelled under ss 75B and 69` `the worker's failure or refusal was unreasonable` `days since I gave notice of the cut` `I gave the s 69 statement`
